---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Our Inspiration | Shashvat Paediatric Care Foundation">
  <!-- Page Header -->
  <div class="relative bg-slate-950 py-8 sm:py-10 overflow-hidden border-b border-orange-900/30">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[url('/assets/images/tmh.jpg')] bg-cover bg-center opacity-10 mix-blend-luminosity"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-slate-950 via-slate-900/80 to-transparent"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center z-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-orange-500/10 border border-orange-500/20 text-orange-400 font-bold text-xs mb-4 uppercase tracking-widest backdrop-blur-sm">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-orange-500 animate-pulse"></span>
        The Heart of Our Mission
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-4">Our Inspiration</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">The story of Shashvat, the little boy whose big dreams inspired our foundation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="py-24 bg-white relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Decorative background elements -->
    <div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-1/3 h-full bg-gradient-to-b from-orange-50/50 to-transparent skew-x-12 transform origin-top translate-x-20"></div>
    <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-64 h-64 bg-amber-50 rounded-full blur-3xl opacity-50"></div>
    
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10">
      <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16 items-start">
        
        <!-- Image Column -->
        <div class="max-w-md mx-auto lg:max-w-none lg:col-span-4 mb-16 lg:mb-0 lg:sticky lg:top-32 relative group">
          <div class="absolute -inset-4 bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-400 to-amber-400 rounded-3xl opacity-20 group-hover:opacity-40 transition duration-500 blur-2xl"></div>
          <div class="relative">
            <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-orange-100 rounded-[2rem] transform -translate-x-4 -translate-y-4 transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:-translate-x-6 group-hover:-translate-y-6"></div>
            <img src="/assets/images/Shashvat.webp" alt="Shashvat" class="relative rounded-[2rem] shadow-2xl object-cover w-full h-auto border-4 border-white transform transition-transform duration-700 group-hover:scale-[1.02]" />
          </div>
          
          <div class="mt-12 text-center relative">
            <svg class="absolute -top-6 left-1/2 transform -translate-x-1/2 w-12 h-12 text-orange-200 opacity-50" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 32 32"><path d="M9.352 4C4.456 7.456 1 13.12 1 19.36c0 5.088 3.072 8.064 6.624 8.064 3.36 0 5.856-2.688 5.856-5.856 0-3.168-2.208-5.472-5.088-5.472-.576 0-1.344.096-1.536.192.48-3.264 3.552-7.104 6.624-9.024L9.352 4zm16.512 0c-4.8 3.456-8.256 9.12-8.256 15.36 0 5.088 3.072 8.064 6.624 8.064 3.264 0 5.856-2.688 5.856-5.856 0-3.168-2.304-5.472-5.184-5.472-.576 0-1.248.096-1.44.192.48-3.264 3.456-7.104 6.528-9.024L25.864 4z"></path></svg>
            <p class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif italic text-slate-700 leading-snug relative z-10">
              "He was and is in true sense <span class="text-orange-600 font-bold">SHASHVAT</span> (eternal)."
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Text Column -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-8">
          <div class="prose prose-lg prose-orange text-slate-600">
            <p class="text-2xl leading-relaxed text-slate-800 font-medium mb-8">
              Shashvat, a sweet little boy with big dreams. He wanted to become a Paediatric Oncologist.
            </p>
            <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
              He did well in whatever that came to his plate in his little lifetime. Be it in his Academics or Roller Skating, Table Tennis, Swimming and lately playing piano, he was good at everything. He had many friends with whom he played, but “Tanmay” was his best friend, the only one he missed a lot in his last days.
            </p>
            <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
              As parents we were so proud of him. He was our Shravan Kumar, who even in his last days, thought about his parents and expressed his gratitude by telling us how lucky he was to get parents like us. However, it was the other way round. For us he is still with us. He was and is in true sense SHASHVAT (eternal).
            </p>
            
            <div class="bg-orange-50 border-l-4 border-orange-500 p-8 rounded-r-2xl my-10 shadow-sm relative overflow-hidden group">
               <div class="absolute right-0 top-0 w-24 h-24 bg-orange-100 rounded-full blur-xl transform translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 group-hover:scale-150 transition-transform duration-700"></div>
              <p class="mb-0 text-slate-700 font-medium relative z-10 text-lg">
                As a child he was very soft spoken, obedient and wonderful kid, but the other side of his personality was full of kindness and empathy, especially towards the underprivileged ones. At the age of 12 he expressed his wish to help children with critical illness and support their families through variable means, a virtue very rarely seen especially at his tender age.
              </p>
            </div>
            
            <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
              This probably came to him because he himself had gone through the sufferings and had a fair idea of what a family goes through during the treatment.
            </p>
            <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
              As parents, we have witnessed the helplessness and agony a family goes through when you see your child in pain and suffering. Every family in such case tries to provide the best treatment available despite being drained out emotionally and financially. Unlike well off families, the underprivileged families also need to take care of the means to feed their family over and above the treatment expenses. Shashvat understood this at very tender age.
            </p>
            
            <hr class="border-slate-200 my-10" />
            
            <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">His Legacy Lives On</h3>
            <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6 text-lg">
              As per Shashvat’s last wish, <strong class="text-orange-600">SHASHVAT PAEDIATRIC CARE FOUNDATION (SPCF)</strong> was founded to take care of critically ill children. SPCF is committed to provide financial assistance to all such children who are coming from underprivileged families. It was formed with an aim that family should focus only on the children, without worrying about the financial part of the treatment.
            </p>
            <p class="leading-relaxed text-lg">
              As a part of this initiative, SPCF has collaborated with National Cancer Institute, Nagpur and Tata Memorial Hospital, Mumbai and trying to serve the children and families through any such opportunities created.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
